Findings  ✗ 0 errors · ⚠ 0 warnings · 3 info

  1  • workflows use variable DEPLOY_ENABLED, but no template or schema
       documents it
       info · EG012 ci-secret-undocumented · .github/workflows/deploy.yml:6:9

     Why      Whoever sets up a fork, a new environment or a new repository has
              to discover DEPLOY_ENABLED by reading workflow files; a missing
              one usually shows up as a failed deploy.
     Fix      Document it: add `DEPLOY_ENABLED=` to .env.example with a comment
              such as
              `# CI: set in GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions (Variables tab)`,
              or declare it under `variables:` in .envguard.yaml.

  2  • workflows use secret DEPLOY_KEY, but no template or schema documents it
       info · EG012 ci-secret-undocumented · .github/workflows/deploy.yml:13:27

     Why      Whoever sets up a fork, a new environment or a new repository has
              to discover DEPLOY_KEY by reading workflow files; a missing one
              usually shows up as a failed deploy.
     Fix      Document it: add `DEPLOY_KEY=` to .env.example with a comment such
              as
              `# CI: set in GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions (Secrets tab)`,
              or declare it under `variables:` in .envguard.yaml.
     Related  .github/workflows/deploy.yml:16:24

